Costs of asthma according to the degree of severity</article-title><source>Eur Respir J</source><year>1998</year><volume>12</volume><fpage>1322</fpage><lpage>1326</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9877485</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b10-copd-4-185"><label>10.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Pauwels</surname><given-names>RA</given-names></name><name><surname>Rabe</surname><given-names>KF</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Burden and clinical features of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD)</article-title><source>Lancet</source><year>2004</year><volume>364</volume><fpage>613</fpage><lpage>620</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15313363</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b11-copd-4-185"><label>11.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cooper</surname><given-names>CB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The connection between chronic obstructive pulmonary disease symptoms and hyperinflation and its impact on exercise and function</article-title><source>Am J Med</source><year>2006</year><volume>119</volume><fpage>21</fpage><lpage>31</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16996896</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b12-copd-4-185"><label>12.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="other"><person-group person-group-type="author"><collab>Global Initiative for Chronic Obstructive Lung Disease</collab></person-group><comment>Global strategy for the diagnosis, management and prevention of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. 2008 Update. <ext-link ext-link-type="uri" xlink:href="www.goldcopd.org">www.goldcopd.org</ext-link>. 2&#x02013;11&#x02013;2008</comment></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b13-copd-4-185"><label>13.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Traver</surname><given-names>GA</given-names></name><name><surname>Cline</surname><given-names>MG</given-names></name><name><surname>Burrows</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Predictors of mortality in chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. A 15-year follow-up study</article-title><source>Am Rev Respir Dis</source><year>1979</year><volume>119</volume><fpage>895</fpage><lpage>902</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">453709</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b14-copd-4-185"><label>14.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schunemann</surname><given-names>HJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Dorn</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Grant</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Winkelstein</surname><given-names>W</given-names><suffix>Jr</suffix></name><name><surname>Trevisan</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Pulmonary function is a long-term predictor of mortality in the general population: 29-year follow-up of the Buffalo Health Study</article-title><source>Chest</source><year>2000</year><volume>118</volume><fpage>656</fpage><lpage>664</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10988186</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b15-copd-4-185"><label>15.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Young</surname><given-names>RP</given-names></name><name><surname>Hopkins</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Eaton</surname><given-names>TE</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Forced expiratory volume in one second: not just a lung function test but a marker of premature death from all causes</article-title><source>Eur Respir J</source><year>2007</year><volume>30</volume><fpage>616</fpage><lpage>622</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">17906084</pub-id></mixed-citation></ref><ref id="b16-copd-4-185"><label>16.</label><mixed-citation publication-type="journal"><pe